    "narrative": "Our top plays for today hinge on favorable leadoff opportunities and exploitable matchups. **Will Smith** (62.94) enters as our strongest start, benefiting significantly from his spot atop the order and a favorable 4.07 xERA matchup against Roupp. Similarly, **Masyn Winn** (62.40) provides excellent value at shortstop; despite facing a lefty, his park factor and elite situational metrics keep him well above the 60-point threshold for a Strong start. **Brendan Donovan** (61.16) also earns a recommendation today, as a 14% boost from his platoon advantage and leadoff deployment against Burrows outweighs his park and SP skill penalties.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Drew Gilbert**, whose 37.35 score left him just shy of our 40-point floor. While his platoon edge against Sheehan was helpful, his placement in the bottom of the order (-6%) and the high xERA of the opposing pitcher stifled his output. **Luis Arraez** (47.91) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (48.85) remain in the lineup despite the tough 3.16 xERA Sheehan provides, as their leadoff and two-hole order protection keeps their floor stable. Conversely, **Gavin Sheets** (42.53) sits on the edge of viability; he will remain active, but he remains the first candidate for pinch-hit replacement should the game state shift.\n\nWe are navigating a tough slate against several pitchers with xERA marks below 3.20. While **Matt Chapman** (43.49) is facing a difficult matchup against Sheehan, his power potential keeps him ahead of the sub-40 group. With **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Geraldo Perdomo** unavailable due to team off-days, our bench is strictly limited to depth pieces like **Wenceel Perez**, whose poor platoon metrics against McLean confirm his status as a bench asset for today. Monitor weather reports for the late games, as any shifts in wind could further impact the viability of our lower-scored starters like **Gavin Sheets**.",
